Critical Rules





Use layered architecture: controller, service, repository, entity packages.



Implement RESTful APIs with proper HTTP methods and status codes (e.g., POST /requests returns 201).



Secure endpoints with Spring Security: JWT authentication, role-based authorization.



Use @RestController for APIs, @Service for business logic, @Repository for data access.



Configure application.properties for database (e.g., H2, MySQL) and server settings.



Use @Entity with JPA annotations for database models; map relationships correctly (e.g., @ManyToOne).



Handle exceptions with @ControllerAdvice and return consistent error responses.



Include logging with SLF4J/Logback; log key actions (e.g., request creation, approval actions).



Write unit tests with JUnit and Mockito for services and controllers.



Avoid hardcoding; use @Value or configuration classes for constants.



Follow Java naming conventions: camelCase for methods/variables, PascalCase for classes.



For request-based approval system:





Implement workflow: Staff → Manager → Director → CEO.



Use enums for statuses (e.g., Pending_Manager, Approved).



Log actions in ApprovalHistory table.

